WEBVTT

﻿1
00:01:08.652 --> 00:01:11.822
Can't we just go home in that?

2
00:01:13.157 --> 00:01:15.325
- Can we?
- Should we ask?

3
00:01:15.326 --> 00:01:18.037
- This is Opera. Fish, do you copy?
- Yes, let's ask.

4
00:01:20.372 --> 00:01:23.875
- Do choppers usually wobble like that?
- This is Opera. Fish, do you copy?

5
00:01:23.876 --> 00:01:25.794
I've never seen one before,
so I'm not sure.

6
00:01:25.795 --> 00:01:28.464
But it is swaying quite a bit, sir.

7
00:01:29.423 --> 00:01:32.509
Maybe it's because the wind
is blowing too strongly.

8
00:01:32.510 --> 00:01:35.346
This is Opera. Fish, do you copy?

9
00:01:37.807 --> 00:01:40.392
This is Opera. Respond, over.

10
00:01:41.268 --> 00:01:43.562
- Kyung-sik!
- Private Hwang Kyung-sik, sir!

11
00:01:45.272 --> 00:01:47.316
- Are they responding?
- Negative, sir.

12
00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:50.235
The pilot seems inexperienced,
so stay alert.

13
00:01:50.236 --> 00:01:51.653
- Yes, sir.
- Sir!

14
00:01:51.654 --> 00:01:53.363
- Don't do it.
- What is it now?

15
00:01:53.364 --> 00:01:54.698
Will you be quiet?

16
00:01:55.407 --> 00:01:56.866
You idiot!

17
00:01:56.867 --> 00:01:57.952
Hey, you punk!

18
00:01:58.744 --> 00:01:59.744
What's he doing?

19
00:01:59.745 --> 00:02:02.039
Don't cross the helipad! Focus, damn it!

20
00:02:03.415 --> 00:02:04.250
You piece of shit!

21
00:02:06.752 --> 00:02:09.380
You cannot let them land, sir!
Look at this!

22
00:02:13.217 --> 00:02:14.218
Shit.

23
00:02:20.266 --> 00:02:21.100
What?

24
00:02:26.772 --> 00:02:28.983
This is Opera. Fish, do you copy?

25
00:02:37.908 --> 00:02:39.826
Can you please just walk straight?

26
00:02:39.827 --> 00:02:42.454
Hold on. Are there any zombies here?

27
00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:44.707
Let's go in here.

28
00:02:45.708 --> 00:02:47.334
Get in there.

29
00:02:50.504 --> 00:02:53.339
- Damn it, go your own way.
- Let me in!

30
00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:54.717
Stop following us.

31
00:03:00.097 --> 00:03:01.098
Shit.

32
00:03:08.564 --> 00:03:09.481
No zombies?

33
00:03:09.982 --> 00:03:11.357
My head is killing me.

34
00:03:11.358 --> 00:03:13.819
Look at that.
They have oriental raisin tea.

35
00:03:17.323 --> 00:03:18.489
Let's drink some more.

36
00:03:18.490 --> 00:03:20.366
- Drink up, Tripeater.
- Okay.

37
00:03:20.367 --> 00:03:21.951
Cheers, Boozer.

38
00:03:21.952 --> 00:03:24.413
- Seriously, they're both crazy.
- Drink up.

39
00:03:27.666 --> 00:03:29.292
- What's going on?
- Fire in the hole!

40
00:03:29.293 --> 00:03:31.128
- Zombies.
- It's zombies!

41
00:03:32.546 --> 00:03:34.672
- Fire in the hole!
- That's freaking sick.

42
00:03:34.673 --> 00:03:36.591
- Hey, that's Alex.
- Where?

43
00:03:36.592 --> 00:03:38.594
- Hi, Alex.
- Alex, over here!

44
00:03:42.056 --> 00:03:43.349
Oh no.

45
00:03:47.311 --> 00:03:49.938
- You killed it!
- That was so dope.

46
00:03:49.939 --> 00:03:51.898
- Let's cheers to that.
- Can we replay that?

47
00:03:51.899 --> 00:03:53.358
This is ridiculous.

48
00:03:53.359 --> 00:03:54.275
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

49
00:03:54.276 --> 00:03:56.362
Lay off the booze, damn it!

50
00:03:56.946 --> 00:03:57.905
You drink this.

51
00:04:00.282 --> 00:04:01.116
Gross.

52
00:04:01.742 --> 00:04:02.784
Damn it.

53
00:04:02.785 --> 00:04:03.785
- Jin-wook!
- Huh?

54
00:04:03.786 --> 00:04:06.079
- Hey, open the door!
- Where's my beer?

55
00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:08.498
- It's Alex.
- What am I? A fucking doormat?

56
00:04:08.499 --> 00:04:10.458
- Fuck.
- I'm coming. Hold on.

57
00:04:10.459 --> 00:04:11.669
Hurry up!

58
00:04:12.836 --> 00:04:15.088
- Quick!
- Alex, come on!

59
00:04:15.089 --> 00:04:16.882
Alex!

60
00:04:17.257 --> 00:04:18.841
I think I drank too much.

61
00:04:18.842 --> 00:04:20.385
- That was awesome.
- Are you guys okay?

62
00:04:20.386 --> 00:04:21.970
Can you do that again?

63
00:04:21.971 --> 00:04:23.555
Look, it's zombies.

64
00:04:24.807 --> 00:04:26.307
- They're baseball players.
- That's it.

65
00:04:26.308 --> 00:04:27.559
They're fighting again.

66
00:04:28.143 --> 00:04:29.560
Go, Twins!

67
00:04:29.561 --> 00:04:32.021
No, the Giants are the best.

68
00:04:32.022 --> 00:04:33.148
You're wrong.

69
00:04:33.524 --> 00:04:35.441
- Get them, Giants!
- Kiwoom Heroes all the way.

70
00:04:35.442 --> 00:04:37.902
- Go, Twins! You can do it!
- Go, Giants!

71
00:04:37.903 --> 00:04:39.029
Let's go!

72
00:04:44.201 --> 00:04:45.411
Raise your rifles!

73
00:04:46.203 --> 00:04:47.912
Lock and load on the chopper!

74
00:04:47.913 --> 00:04:49.415
Air defense squad, to your positions!

75
00:05:01.677 --> 00:05:02.970
- What?
- What?

76
00:05:03.679 --> 00:05:04.638
To your positions!

77
00:05:06.098 --> 00:05:06.932
To your positions!

78
00:05:08.809 --> 00:05:13.188
Target approaching at four o'clock!

79
00:05:20.112 --> 00:05:21.863
This is as far as it will go, sir.

80
00:05:21.864 --> 00:05:23.157
Prepare to fire!

81
00:05:23.532 --> 00:05:25.826
Engage the chopper's tail!

82
00:05:29.913 --> 00:05:32.290
- Damn it.
- Get it together!

83
00:05:32.291 --> 00:05:34.001
Do you want to go home in a box?

84
00:05:37.254 --> 00:05:38.337
Shit.

85
00:05:38.338 --> 00:05:40.048
Aim and fire!

86
00:05:40.049 --> 00:05:43.051
- Aim and fire!
- Aim and fire!

87
00:05:43.052 --> 00:05:44.261
Aim and fire!

88
00:05:52.102 --> 00:05:53.186
Get the tail!

89
00:05:53.187 --> 00:05:55.021
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

90
00:05:55.022 --> 00:05:57.024
Private Ra In-ho, aiming at the tail!

91
00:06:01.862 --> 00:06:04.156
- Is it within range?
- Closing in, sir!

92
00:06:08.368 --> 00:06:09.535
Shoot it down!

93
00:06:09.536 --> 00:06:11.496
Target locked! One, two!

94
00:06:11.497 --> 00:06:12.623
Commencing fire!

95
00:06:51.745 --> 00:06:53.247
I feel like shit.

96
00:06:58.585 --> 00:07:00.921
Hey, what's that?

97
00:07:05.175 --> 00:07:07.344
There's no time for this. Lead the way.

98
00:07:10.347 --> 00:07:11.306
They're gone.

99
00:07:14.393 --> 00:07:16.228
- Get Young-joo.
- Come here.

100
00:07:17.062 --> 00:07:18.855
- I feel horrible.
- Watch your step.

101
00:07:18.856 --> 00:07:20.815
- Look at that.
- Hang in there, okay?

102
00:07:20.816 --> 00:07:22.818
Damn, I feel like throwing up.

103
00:07:23.569 --> 00:07:24.570
Let's hurry.

104
00:07:25.028 --> 00:07:28.365
Who cares how much a chopper costs
in this situation?

105
00:07:28.866 --> 00:07:31.534
<i>Did you just yell at me?
Are you fucking crazy?</i>

106
00:07:31.535 --> 00:07:32.911
<i>Get your head straight!</i>

107
00:07:34.413 --> 00:07:35.455
I'm sorry, sir.

108
00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:40.835
Battalion Commander,
if you can't send us supplies,

109
00:07:40.836 --> 00:07:44.882
please allow us to relocate
to the base camp at Suseo Station.

110
00:07:45.924 --> 00:07:48.342
If we stay here,
we'll run out of food and water.

111
00:07:48.343 --> 00:07:50.178
We won't last more than a few days.

112
00:07:50.179 --> 00:07:53.764
We'll figure out a way to join the ranks
at Suseo Station's base camp--

113
00:07:53.765 --> 00:07:57.186
<i>Negative. Cut the nonsense
and stand by at your current location.</i>

114
00:07:57.728 --> 00:07:58.686
Yes, sir.

115
00:07:58.687 --> 00:08:00.646
<i>I'll monitor the situation
and get back to you.</i>

116
00:08:00.647 --> 00:08:01.815
<i>Until then, stand by.</i>

117
00:08:02.274 --> 00:08:03.609
Yes, sir. Understood.

118
00:08:04.735 --> 00:08:05.736
Salute.

119
00:08:08.238 --> 00:08:09.573
That fucking bastard.

120
00:08:10.532 --> 00:08:14.077
Is he telling us to stay holed up
in this fucking place and die?

121
00:08:16.455 --> 00:08:17.998
All right, listen up.

122
00:08:19.291 --> 00:08:21.084
Here's the bottom line.

123
00:08:23.503 --> 00:08:25.130
We're leaving this building today.

124
00:08:25.672 --> 00:08:27.174
- What?
- Sir?

125
00:08:29.134 --> 00:08:31.344
Is it to get supplies from the brigade?

126
00:08:31.345 --> 00:08:34.973
Unfortunately,
there won't be any resupply.

127
00:08:37.226 --> 00:08:40.353
We can go a few weeks without food, sir.

128
00:08:40.354 --> 00:08:42.897
That's right, sir.
We still have running water.

129
00:08:42.898 --> 00:08:45.525
I know there's enough water
in the hotel water tank.

130
00:08:46.318 --> 00:08:48.403
But we'll lose power in a few days.

131
00:08:48.987 --> 00:08:52.365
When that happens,
it'll cut off our water supply.

132
00:08:52.366 --> 00:08:56.786
If that's the case,
can't we leave when the water is cut off?

133
00:08:56.787 --> 00:08:57.704
Sir?

134
00:09:00.499 --> 00:09:03.542
Do you think we can put up a fight
on just water alone?

135
00:09:03.543 --> 00:09:04.920
Dang it.

136
00:09:05.295 --> 00:09:08.590
It's better to make a move
while we still have the energy left.

137
00:09:09.383 --> 00:09:10.842
Since it's come down to this,

138
00:09:11.718 --> 00:09:15.639
our only option is to fight like hell
to make it out of here alive.

139
00:09:19.142 --> 00:09:20.018
What is it?

140
00:09:23.814 --> 00:09:24.731
May I...

141
00:09:26.275 --> 00:09:27.442
have a gun?

142
00:09:30.362 --> 00:09:31.821
Given the situation we're in,

143
00:09:31.822 --> 00:09:34.824
I'm really trying to go easy on you
about what happened last night.

144
00:09:34.825 --> 00:09:36.158
So please don't cross the line.

145
00:09:36.159 --> 00:09:38.453
Didn't you see me shoot yesterday?

146
00:09:39.079 --> 00:09:43.416
I competed as a shooter in high school
and made it to the national reserve team.

147
00:09:43.417 --> 00:09:47.629
I'm pretty sure I'm a better shooter
than most of the men here.

148
00:09:48.088 --> 00:09:50.132
You can test me if you want.

149
00:09:50.882 --> 00:09:52.134
Please let me...

150
00:09:54.594 --> 00:09:56.305
fight for my own life.

151
00:09:59.308 --> 00:10:00.933
- Damn.
- Holy shit.

152
00:10:00.934 --> 00:10:02.226
- Shit.
- Unbelievable.

153
00:10:02.227 --> 00:10:04.021
What the hell?

154
00:10:06.648 --> 00:10:08.275
I can't believe this is Gangnam.

155
00:10:11.486 --> 00:10:13.196
This isn't what I expected to see.

156
00:10:14.156 --> 00:10:15.907
This place has been wiped out, too.

157
00:10:19.161 --> 00:10:21.620
Damn it, what a fucking grand reception.

158
00:10:21.621 --> 00:10:23.707
911 EMERGENCY

159
00:10:24.750 --> 00:10:26.709
It seems they called an ambulance.

160
00:10:26.710 --> 00:10:28.754
Are you sure there are soldiers here?

161
00:10:33.633 --> 00:10:34.843
Jae-yoon.

162
00:10:35.761 --> 00:10:39.097
Hey, where are you going?
You're not going in there, are you?

163
00:10:39.556 --> 00:10:42.099
Are you out of your mind?
Don't you see that?

164
00:10:42.100 --> 00:10:43.685
- Are you trying to get killed?
- Hey.

165
00:10:45.645 --> 00:10:46.896
He's right, though.

166
00:10:46.897 --> 00:10:49.023
We'll die if we go in now.

167
00:10:49.024 --> 00:10:52.151
Let's go somewhere safe
and wait to hear from your boyfriend.

168
00:10:52.152 --> 00:10:54.653
Okay? I'm sure he'll call you.

169
00:10:54.654 --> 00:10:56.531
Let's go down to the parking lot for now.

170
00:10:57.282 --> 00:11:00.535
Yeah, don't worry too much.
Let's just go for now.

171
00:11:04.373 --> 00:11:07.249
Come on, let's go.
You can't get through that.

172
00:11:07.250 --> 00:11:09.795
He's right. Come on, Boozer. Let's go.

173
00:11:10.420 --> 00:11:11.505
Come on.

174
00:11:12.839 --> 00:11:14.507
They drove right into the middle.

175
00:11:14.508 --> 00:11:17.426
- Jae-yoon.
- It's like a zombie convention, right?

176
00:11:17.427 --> 00:11:20.012
Shit, what a mess.

177
00:11:20.013 --> 00:11:22.515
- Is this the only way in?
- It's a fucking mess.

178
00:11:22.516 --> 00:11:24.642
It looks like a hiding spot for zombies.

179
00:11:24.643 --> 00:11:27.144
- Is there anything in the car?
- Look at all this blood.

180
00:11:27.145 --> 00:11:28.437
It's empty.

181
00:11:28.438 --> 00:11:31.149
- Are you sure about this?
- Hey, slow down.

182
00:11:39.866 --> 00:11:41.076
Hold on.

183
00:11:41.952 --> 00:11:46.372
Let's split up and look for my car.
It's a navy Hummer. Plate number 4574.

184
00:11:46.373 --> 00:11:49.250
- Are you sure it's in this zone?
- I don't know.

185
00:11:49.251 --> 00:11:51.002
A navy Hummer. Plate number 4574.

186
00:11:53.130 --> 00:11:56.424
How can you not remember
where you parked your own car?

187
00:11:56.425 --> 00:11:58.467
I used the valet service
because I'm a VVIP.

188
00:11:58.468 --> 00:12:00.344
- About earlier...
- What's a "VVIP"?

189
00:12:00.345 --> 00:12:02.639
- "Very, Very Important Person."
- Sorry I lost my temper.

190
00:12:03.515 --> 00:12:04.933
But you know...

191
00:12:05.642 --> 00:12:08.394
You were in the wrong.
You'd be dead if you went inside.

192
00:12:08.395 --> 00:12:10.604
- Hey, what's that?
- You know that, right?

193
00:12:10.605 --> 00:12:11.647
- Young-joo!
- Run!

194
00:12:11.648 --> 00:12:14.067
- Move! Hurry!
- Get out of there!

195
00:12:15.152 --> 00:12:17.070
- The zombies are coming!
- Fuck!

196
00:12:19.156 --> 00:12:20.532
Run!

197
00:12:26.830 --> 00:12:27.747
No.

198
00:12:28.165 --> 00:12:29.416
What the fuck?

199
00:12:30.333 --> 00:12:32.626
Get away from me, you piece of shit!

200
00:12:32.627 --> 00:12:33.753
Go away!

201
00:12:50.854 --> 00:12:52.898
Young-joo!

202
00:13:17.672 --> 00:13:20.466
- Alex!
- Hey, stop! That's suicide!

203
00:13:20.467 --> 00:13:22.677
Let go, Jin-wook!

204
00:13:25.013 --> 00:13:26.848
Just fucking listen to me, damn it!

205
00:13:27.724 --> 00:13:29.392
No, Alex!

206
00:13:31.811 --> 00:13:33.687
- No.
- Die!

207
00:13:33.688 --> 00:13:35.690
No! Alex!

208
00:13:40.237 --> 00:13:42.113
Alex!

209
00:13:43.198 --> 00:13:45.616
No! Please!

210
00:13:45.617 --> 00:13:47.827
No!

211
00:14:13.144 --> 00:14:15.897
I know you're all scared.

212
00:14:17.148 --> 00:14:19.316
But we have to overcome this.

213
00:14:19.317 --> 00:14:20.860
Why is that, Hwang Kyung-sik?

214
00:14:21.361 --> 00:14:22.653
Private Hwang Kyung-sik.

215
00:14:22.654 --> 00:14:25.156
It's because we serve
the Republic of Korea, sir.

216
00:14:26.533 --> 00:14:28.660
Save that for the president.

217
00:14:30.829 --> 00:14:31.870
Yes, sir!

218
00:14:31.871 --> 00:14:33.623
Do you know what true victory is?

219
00:14:35.709 --> 00:14:38.670
It's to survive.
Survival is the ultimate victory.

220
00:14:40.922 --> 00:14:44.133
"To live, you must be willing to die.
To fear death is to ensure it."

221
00:14:44.134 --> 00:14:45.093
What does that mean?

222
00:14:52.017 --> 00:14:55.604
It means we need to fight to survive.
If we hold back in fear, we'll die.

223
00:14:56.313 --> 00:14:57.272
Correct.

224
00:15:00.734 --> 00:15:04.486
We fight to the death
so we can make it back home.

225
00:15:04.487 --> 00:15:06.363
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

226
00:15:06.364 --> 00:15:07.907
That's the spirit.

227
00:15:08.617 --> 00:15:13.287
We'll take the stairs to the VIP lounge.

228
00:15:13.288 --> 00:15:14.998
From there, we'll take the elevator.

229
00:15:16.291 --> 00:15:17.876
Okay, let's head out.

230
00:15:22.881 --> 00:15:24.590
Kim Young-man, Kwak Gye-young.
Get the door.

231
00:15:24.591 --> 00:15:25.884
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

232
00:15:29.137 --> 00:15:31.347
Hold fire until I give the order.
Understood?

233
00:15:31.348 --> 00:15:32.432
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

234
00:15:32.932 --> 00:15:35.060
- Selector switch to semi.
- Switching to semi.

235
00:15:36.186 --> 00:15:37.478
On the count of three.

236
00:15:37.479 --> 00:15:38.396
One.

237
00:15:40.023 --> 00:15:40.857
Two.

238
00:15:42.359 --> 00:15:43.193
Three.

239
00:15:49.074 --> 00:15:50.492
Shit, what's this smell?

240
00:15:52.160 --> 00:15:53.870
What is all this?

241
00:16:52.512 --> 00:16:53.555
Hey!

242
00:16:54.806 --> 00:16:58.143
I don't think the car's over here!
Go check if it's in another zone!

243
00:17:03.314 --> 00:17:04.149
What's he doing?

244
00:17:10.113 --> 00:17:10.947
Loser.

245
00:17:12.949 --> 00:17:15.117
What the fuck is wrong with you,
you fucking bastard?

246
00:17:15.118 --> 00:17:17.911
I'm going to kill you
when I get my hands on you!

247
00:17:17.912 --> 00:17:19.831
You fucking piece of shit!

248
00:17:20.832 --> 00:17:23.375
So, what do you want me to do?

249
00:17:23.376 --> 00:17:25.211
Why you little...

250
00:17:27.756 --> 00:17:32.593
Just go look for the car.
When you find it, bring it over here.

251
00:17:32.594 --> 00:17:33.927
I don't know how to drive.

252
00:17:33.928 --> 00:17:36.430
Why the hell didn't you get your license?

253
00:17:36.431 --> 00:17:38.432
I was trying to get into college!

254
00:17:38.433 --> 00:17:40.392
Keep this up, and I'm out of here.

255
00:17:40.393 --> 00:17:42.102
Okay, I'm sorry. Just hold on.

256
00:17:42.103 --> 00:17:43.188
Hold on, damn it!

257
00:17:47.233 --> 00:17:49.903
Your phone's not dead, right?

258
00:17:50.487 --> 00:17:52.404
- Give me your number.
- What?

259
00:17:52.405 --> 00:17:53.490
Your phone number.

260
00:18:00.371 --> 00:18:02.749
- Keep your guard up.
- Be careful, sir.

261
00:18:03.249 --> 00:18:04.375
Are they dead now?

262
00:18:09.714 --> 00:18:10.924
Pick up the pace.

263
00:19:01.432 --> 00:19:02.600
This is fucked up.

264
00:19:03.184 --> 00:19:06.061
We're in the thick of it,
and he's hung up over the chopper's cost?

265
00:19:06.062 --> 00:19:09.232
What about the cost of the chopper, sir?

266
00:19:09.941 --> 00:19:12.442
He wants us to pay
for the chopper you shot down.

267
00:19:12.443 --> 00:19:14.486
Oh, that supply chopper?

268
00:19:14.487 --> 00:19:17.115
You're all accomplices,
so we're splitting the cost.

269
00:19:18.199 --> 00:19:19.575
- But...
- Do I have to pay?

270
00:19:19.576 --> 00:19:20.909
How much is a chopper?

271
00:19:20.910 --> 00:19:23.161
- I don't know, sir.
- We're screwed.

272
00:19:23.162 --> 00:19:25.163
- Shit.
- Do I really have to pay?

273
00:19:25.164 --> 00:19:26.332
It was a joke.

274
00:19:34.090 --> 00:19:38.469
Before we head down to the lobby,
we'll sweep the lounge in pairs.

275
00:19:39.888 --> 00:19:43.223
If the coast is clear,
proceed with weapons maintenance.

276
00:19:43.224 --> 00:19:47.519
The condition of your firearms
will dictate how the next fight goes.

277
00:19:47.520 --> 00:19:49.938
Once that's done, we'll head to the lobby.

278
00:19:49.939 --> 00:19:52.149
- Do you understand?
- Yes, sir.

279
00:19:52.150 --> 00:19:55.027
Then start the sweep. Go.

280
00:19:55.028 --> 00:19:56.403
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

281
00:19:56.404 --> 00:19:57.697
You're with me.

282
00:20:10.960 --> 00:20:12.545
How am I supposed to find it?

283
00:20:13.463 --> 00:20:14.631
This is just...

284
00:20:20.470 --> 00:20:21.471
What the hell?

285
00:20:23.681 --> 00:20:25.390
304NO 4574

286
00:20:25.391 --> 00:20:27.727
Oh, that's it. That's the car.

287
00:20:29.187 --> 00:20:31.981
Plate number 4574. Yes!

288
00:20:32.899 --> 00:20:33.858
Oh, god.

289
00:20:34.359 --> 00:20:36.777
Sorry, zombies.
Can you get out of the way?

290
00:20:36.778 --> 00:20:38.279
Excuse me.

291
00:20:40.031 --> 00:20:42.450
Go away. There's nothing here.

292
00:20:51.626 --> 00:20:52.584
BOOZER

293
00:20:52.585 --> 00:20:54.211
I have no idea how this works.

294
00:20:54.212 --> 00:20:56.839
VIDEO CALL
BOOZER

295
00:20:57.298 --> 00:20:59.216
- Hello?
<i>- Are you in the car?</i>

296
00:20:59.217 --> 00:21:01.886
- Yes.
<i>- Can you start the engine?</i>

297
00:21:02.428 --> 00:21:04.972
No, I told you.
I did nothing but work and study.

298
00:21:04.973 --> 00:21:07.975
Seriously?
Press the "engine start" button.

299
00:21:07.976 --> 00:21:09.519
The "engine start" button?

300
00:21:12.105 --> 00:21:13.188
I don't see it.

301
00:21:13.189 --> 00:21:16.233
<i>If it's a Hummer, you need the key.
Insert it and give it a turn.</i>

302
00:21:16.234 --> 00:21:17.151
Okay.

303
00:21:20.822 --> 00:21:21.947
<i>Is the engine running?</i>

304
00:21:21.948 --> 00:21:24.992
No, not yet. It's not working.

305
00:21:24.993 --> 00:21:27.786
<i>- Why isn't it working?</i>
- Why won't it work?

306
00:21:27.787 --> 00:21:30.706
<i>- Step on the brake.
- You didn't step on the brake?</i>

307
00:21:30.707 --> 00:21:34.042
You didn't tell me to do that.

308
00:21:34.043 --> 00:21:36.712
So, which one is the brake?
There are two pedals.

309
00:21:36.713 --> 00:21:38.131
<i>The left one, damn it!</i>

310
00:21:39.924 --> 00:21:42.677
I swear I'm going to get my license
as soon as this is over.

311
00:21:45.263 --> 00:21:46.556
Okay, what's next?

312
00:21:47.390 --> 00:21:50.851
<i>Put the gear in drive
and step on the right pedal.</i>

313
00:21:50.852 --> 00:21:54.230
Hang on. I can't hold the phone
and grab the wheel at the same time.

314
00:21:56.107 --> 00:21:57.066
There we go.

315
00:21:57.692 --> 00:21:59.735
- Do I put on the seat belt?
<i>- Do whatever you want.</i>

316
00:21:59.736 --> 00:22:01.029
<i>- Just put it on.</i>
- Okay.

317
00:22:02.780 --> 00:22:05.533
He's acting so cocky
just because he knows how to drive.

318
00:22:05.950 --> 00:22:07.285
What an asshole.

319
00:22:07.910 --> 00:22:08.870
I'll be there soon.

320
00:22:11.330 --> 00:22:13.081
Oh, fuck! Is this going to blow up?

321
00:22:13.082 --> 00:22:14.374
<i>What happened?</i>

322
00:22:14.375 --> 00:22:17.502
<i>Take your foot off the brake, dumbass!</i>

323
00:22:17.503 --> 00:22:19.463
<i>And lightly step on the gas.</i>

324
00:22:19.464 --> 00:22:20.631
Fuck.

325
00:22:24.260 --> 00:22:26.804
Holy shit! I'm fucking driving.

326
00:22:27.930 --> 00:22:30.475
Sorry, guys! I'm sorry!

327
00:22:31.642 --> 00:22:33.310
Oh, shit.

328
00:22:33.311 --> 00:22:36.606
This is going too fucking fast!

329
00:22:37.231 --> 00:22:38.149
Help!

330
00:22:39.317 --> 00:22:41.359
Do something!

331
00:22:41.360 --> 00:22:44.905
- Don't jerk the wheel like that!
<i>- I think I'm going to crash!</i>

332
00:22:44.906 --> 00:22:46.490
- Be quiet.
<i>- This is going too fast!</i>

333
00:22:46.491 --> 00:22:48.366
- Don't jerk the wheel so much.
<i>- No, wait!</i>

334
00:22:48.367 --> 00:22:50.786
Hey, are you listening to me?

335
00:22:50.787 --> 00:22:53.330
- Hey!
- Keep your voice down.

336
00:22:53.331 --> 00:22:55.917
Go slow and use the brake.

337
00:23:17.772 --> 00:23:20.023
Private Lee, if we find a zombie here--

338
00:23:20.024 --> 00:23:21.775
Keep your mouth shut.

339
00:23:21.776 --> 00:23:22.860
Yes, sir.

340
00:23:37.375 --> 00:23:38.501
In-ho.

341
00:23:40.878 --> 00:23:43.923
Tell the admin supply officer
that the restrooms are clear.

342
00:23:46.551 --> 00:23:48.386
I have a more pressing matter, sir.

343
00:24:02.233 --> 00:24:03.608
- Sir.
- What?

344
00:24:03.609 --> 00:24:06.153
There are food supplies here
and on the other end.

345
00:24:06.154 --> 00:24:07.113
Okay.

346
00:24:16.080 --> 00:24:18.291
We don't know how long
we'll be in isolation.

347
00:24:20.126 --> 00:24:22.377
Grab food that is light and calorie-dense.

348
00:24:22.378 --> 00:24:24.754
Have everyone put some in their gear
before we head down.

349
00:24:24.755 --> 00:24:26.132
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

350
00:24:27.133 --> 00:24:29.969
- Oh, nice. I'm taking the nuts.
- Bananas...

351
00:24:33.723 --> 00:24:35.391
- Private Lee.
- What?

352
00:24:36.392 --> 00:24:37.393
Sir.

353
00:24:38.853 --> 00:24:39.854
This is for you.

354
00:24:40.438 --> 00:24:42.607
It was smart of you to
pack these red ginseng extracts.

355
00:24:43.149 --> 00:24:45.568
You've got it covered
when it comes to things like this.

356
00:24:56.078 --> 00:24:57.413
{\an8}MY WIFE

357
00:24:59.081 --> 00:25:00.373
{\an8}- Private Lee.
- What?

358
00:25:00.374 --> 00:25:01.583
{\an8}We have Wi-Fi.

359
00:25:01.584 --> 00:25:02.834
{\an8}- What?
- We have Wi-Fi.

360
00:25:02.835 --> 00:25:04.128
We have Wi-Fi?

361
00:25:06.088 --> 00:25:08.883
The Wi-Fi is working. Hold on.

362
00:25:10.635 --> 00:25:12.386
{\an8}MY DARLING YOUNG-JOO

363
00:25:15.514 --> 00:25:17.767
- That's it. Take it slow.
- Take your time.

364
00:25:20.394 --> 00:25:21.354
SWEET JAE-YOON

365
00:25:23.189 --> 00:25:24.023
What the...

366
00:25:26.108 --> 00:25:27.359
Young-joo!

367
00:25:27.360 --> 00:25:28.777
Jae-yoon!

368
00:25:28.778 --> 00:25:30.487
<i>Are you okay? Are you hurt?</i>

369
00:25:30.488 --> 00:25:32.781
No, I'm okay.

370
00:25:32.782 --> 00:25:34.908
- Oh, thank god!
<i>- Are you okay?</i>

371
00:25:34.909 --> 00:25:36.493
<i>- Are you hurt?</i>
- No, I'm fine.

372
00:25:36.494 --> 00:25:38.829
I'm not hurt at all. Look.

373
00:25:39.580 --> 00:25:41.414
- I'm so relieved.
<i>- Where are you?</i>

374
00:25:41.415 --> 00:25:45.126
I'm in the basement of A Tower.
Are you still up there?

375
00:25:45.127 --> 00:25:46.169
What?

376
00:25:46.170 --> 00:25:48.713
<i>What floor are you on? I'll come up.</i>

377
00:25:48.714 --> 00:25:51.800
- Wait--
<i>- Just tell me, and I'll come to you.</i>

378
00:25:51.801 --> 00:25:54.386
Why on earth would you come here?

379
00:25:54.387 --> 00:25:56.179
<i>I was worried about you.</i>

380
00:25:56.180 --> 00:25:59.307
You shouldn't have come here, Young-joo.

381
00:25:59.308 --> 00:26:02.018
<i>Just tell me what floor you're on.</i>

382
00:26:02.019 --> 00:26:06.356
It's really dangerous here,
so you need to go somewhere safe.

383
00:26:06.357 --> 00:26:08.441
Hey, I can't just leave you here.

384
00:26:08.442 --> 00:26:10.694
- Just wait. I'm coming up.
<i>- No, please don't.</i>

385
00:26:10.695 --> 00:26:13.739
You can't do that.
It's really dangerous here!

386
00:26:14.532 --> 00:26:17.993
You have no idea
what I've been through.

387
00:26:17.994 --> 00:26:20.620
<i>I'm super strong. I'm stronger than you.</i>

388
00:26:20.621 --> 00:26:22.163
<i>I'll protect you.</i>

389
00:26:22.164 --> 00:26:23.915
- Oh, come on.
<i>- I'll come to you.</i>

390
00:26:23.916 --> 00:26:25.960
<i>So just tell me where you are.</i>

391
00:26:27.878 --> 00:26:30.672
- Hold on. Hey, Young-joo.
<i>- Yes?</i>

392
00:26:30.673 --> 00:26:32.258
I'm really sorry,

393
00:26:32.842 --> 00:26:37.305
but I forgot to tell you
that I'm not at A Tower right now.

394
00:26:38.014 --> 00:26:39.849
- What?
<i>- So don't stay here...</i>

395
00:26:41.058 --> 00:26:43.768
<i>- I mean, don't stay there--
- Suseo Station.</i>

396
00:26:43.769 --> 00:26:46.146
The Capital Defense Command
is setting up a base camp there.

397
00:26:46.147 --> 00:26:48.606
That's what the first sergeant said
when he was talking to HQ.

398
00:26:48.607 --> 00:26:50.943
<i>- Jae-yoon?</i>
- Go to Suseo Station.

399
00:26:51.694 --> 00:26:52.527
Suseo Station?

400
00:26:52.528 --> 00:26:55.113
That area is full of soldiers,
so it's the safest place.

401
00:26:55.114 --> 00:26:57.574
Head over there,
and I'll be right behind you.

402
00:26:57.575 --> 00:26:59.993
<i>- Okay? I'll see you there.</i>
- Jae-yoon.

403
00:26:59.994 --> 00:27:01.454
{\an8}<i>-Young-joo, Suseo--</i>
- Suseo...

404
00:27:06.917 --> 00:27:08.336
Fuck!

405
00:27:12.048 --> 00:27:13.215
Jae-yoon.

406
00:27:13.549 --> 00:27:15.468
What the fuck?

407
00:27:17.636 --> 00:27:19.472
- Private Lee--
- Hold on.

408
00:27:20.097 --> 00:27:21.890
YOUNG-JOO, THE CALL GOT CUT...

409
00:27:21.891 --> 00:27:24.518
It's a relief nothing bad happened to her.

410
00:27:25.936 --> 00:27:28.063
If she's made it this far,

411
00:27:28.064 --> 00:27:31.692
doesn't that mean
her chances of survival are good?

412
00:27:33.652 --> 00:27:36.864
You're right, In-ho.
That gives me something to hold on to.

413
00:27:38.699 --> 00:27:41.369
I just need to get out of here
and find Young-joo.

414
00:27:47.083 --> 00:27:48.958
- What was that?
- Private Lee.

415
00:27:48.959 --> 00:27:49.960
What happened?

416
00:27:53.297 --> 00:27:55.383
What the heck? Why is it not connecting?

417
00:27:55.800 --> 00:27:57.217
Was the call disconnected?

418
00:27:57.218 --> 00:27:59.011
Hello? Hey!

419
00:28:00.554 --> 00:28:01.806
Damn it.

420
00:28:02.640 --> 00:28:05.684
I'm going way too fast.

421
00:28:06.060 --> 00:28:08.561
I need to slow down,
or I'm going to crash.

422
00:28:08.562 --> 00:28:11.774
I want to get off.
I can't do this anymore.

423
00:28:20.116 --> 00:28:21.742
What was that noise?

424
00:28:24.286 --> 00:28:26.580
- Get up, sir!
- What was that, Sergeant Kim?

425
00:28:28.082 --> 00:28:30.418
- What happened?
- Oh, hey.

426
00:28:31.460 --> 00:28:34.295
Kyung-sik and I took out four zombies.

427
00:28:34.296 --> 00:28:36.714
You're the best, Sergeant Kim.

428
00:28:36.715 --> 00:28:39.008
Don't let your guard down.
They jump out of nowhere.

429
00:28:39.009 --> 00:28:41.344
- Yes, sir.
- They just appeared suddenly.

430
00:28:41.345 --> 00:28:43.596
- Remember, aim for the head.
- Yes, sir.

431
00:28:43.597 --> 00:28:46.182
The zombies came from up there,
but Kyung-sik and I got them all.

432
00:28:46.183 --> 00:28:48.561
- How many did you get?
- That's not important!

433
00:29:02.741 --> 00:29:05.453
- What the fuck?
- We need to move out.

434
00:29:08.914 --> 00:29:10.832
Damn, I must've slipped.

435
00:29:10.833 --> 00:29:12.918
- We should go, sir.
- Okay.

436
00:29:17.965 --> 00:29:20.508
- I should take this, too.
- Something light...

437
00:29:20.509 --> 00:29:22.887
- Papayas.
- This looks tasty.

438
00:29:23.512 --> 00:29:25.930
- Oh, there's bread.
- Stop.

439
00:29:25.931 --> 00:29:27.475
- Stop!
- What?

440
00:29:28.726 --> 00:29:30.727
Hey, wait. Soo-jeong!

441
00:29:30.728 --> 00:29:32.646
- Wait.
- Stop, Paolo!

442
00:29:33.397 --> 00:29:36.816
What are you doing?
Don't you know soldiers can't be in here?

443
00:29:36.817 --> 00:29:39.111
- Paolo.
- What?

444
00:29:40.154 --> 00:29:41.488
- Paolo?
- Gye-young.

445
00:29:41.489 --> 00:29:43.323
- Do not move!
- Sir.

446
00:29:43.324 --> 00:29:44.532
Please don't shoot me.

447
00:29:44.533 --> 00:29:45.451
Paolo.

448
00:29:47.286 --> 00:29:48.829
Are you okay? Were you bitten?

449
00:29:49.663 --> 00:29:50.623
Bitten?

450
00:29:58.464 --> 00:30:01.008
- Tell him I need to check for bite marks.
- Okay.

451
00:30:05.679 --> 00:30:08.015
- Gye-young.
- Yes, sir. Paolo.

452
00:30:09.099 --> 00:30:10.351
He looks fine.

453
00:30:11.560 --> 00:30:13.478
Are you here alone?

454
00:30:13.479 --> 00:30:15.230
Yes, I'm alone.

455
00:30:15.231 --> 00:30:17.525
People were fighting like crazy.

456
00:30:19.401 --> 00:30:21.654
How were you asleep
with all that noise out there?

457
00:30:26.951 --> 00:30:27.785
Are you on drugs?

458
00:30:28.744 --> 00:30:32.413
How can a chef
be doing this sort of thing?

459
00:30:32.414 --> 00:30:34.290
These aren't drugs.
They're sleeping pills.

460
00:30:34.291 --> 00:30:35.416
Sleeping pills?

461
00:30:35.417 --> 00:30:38.211
Hey, First Sergeant, I'm scared.

462
00:30:38.212 --> 00:30:40.839
I want to go to the embassy.
Will you take me there?

463
00:30:41.423 --> 00:30:42.800
We're not going there.

464
00:30:43.342 --> 00:30:45.969
If you rescue a US citizen,
you have to take them to the US embassy.

465
00:30:45.970 --> 00:30:48.388
We're not here to rescue you, Paolo.

466
00:30:48.389 --> 00:30:52.183
Is this how you treat a US citizen?
<i>Jeokbanhajang!</i>

467
00:30:52.184 --> 00:30:53.685
{\an8}JEOKBANHAJANG:
BLAMING THE VICTIM

468
00:30:53.686 --> 00:30:55.770
{\an8}It's not a rescue mission. The embassy?

469
00:30:55.771 --> 00:30:57.439
Don't you know what's going on out there?

470
00:30:57.815 --> 00:31:00.233
- No, it's fine.
- Stop!

471
00:31:00.234 --> 00:31:02.443
Sir, I think he slept through it all.

472
00:31:02.444 --> 00:31:05.114
He doesn't seem to know
what's going on, sir.

473
00:31:05.781 --> 00:31:08.117
Paolo, what's going on?

474
00:31:08.617 --> 00:31:11.287
I want to get off. Get me out of here.

475
00:31:36.145 --> 00:31:39.272
Hey, get out of the way! It's dangerous!

476
00:31:39.273 --> 00:31:41.566
Get out of the way.

477
00:31:41.567 --> 00:31:43.485
You guys should be more careful!

478
00:31:58.876 --> 00:31:59.835
Get off me.

479
00:32:06.967 --> 00:32:08.719
I feel like puking.

480
00:32:10.054 --> 00:32:12.765
Get in the back seat.
I'll take it from here.

481
00:32:15.059 --> 00:32:17.061
Get out of the way, you bastards!

482
00:32:19.563 --> 00:32:20.648
Die!

483
00:32:23.901 --> 00:32:25.860
Die, you fucking bastards!

484
00:32:25.861 --> 00:32:28.529
- Stop it!
- You fucking zombies!

485
00:32:28.530 --> 00:32:30.114
I'm going to puke.

486
00:32:30.115 --> 00:32:32.200
- Die!
- I'm dizzy!

487
00:32:32.201 --> 00:32:33.661
She says she's dizzy!

488
00:32:34.662 --> 00:32:36.413
I'm begging you. Stop the car!

489
00:32:38.040 --> 00:32:39.540
- Damn you all.
- Stop it!

490
00:32:39.541 --> 00:32:42.670
Will you stop?
You're acting like a psycho!

491
00:32:45.881 --> 00:32:48.133
Wouldn't it be better
to live like a psycho?

492
00:32:48.467 --> 00:32:50.885
Well, I want to stay alive
one way or another.

493
00:32:50.886 --> 00:32:53.138
But you need to stop.
It's making her dizzy.

494
00:32:54.431 --> 00:32:57.684
Do you want to be acknowledged
for finding this damn car?

495
00:32:57.685 --> 00:33:01.980
Did you fucking forget
we saved your sorry ass from the streets?

496
00:33:03.065 --> 00:33:05.567
Know your place, Tripeater.

497
00:33:06.568 --> 00:33:10.238
Do your parents know
you're out there getting wasted?

498
00:33:10.239 --> 00:33:13.117
That's why you're not in college yet.

499
00:33:13.826 --> 00:33:17.496
I feel sorry for your parents.
To think they raised you.

500
00:33:18.664 --> 00:33:21.207
What the fuck, man?
I'm going to kill you if you don't let go.

501
00:33:21.208 --> 00:33:25.002
You're the one who's got a death wish.
Should I leave you some teeth marks?

502
00:33:25.003 --> 00:33:28.297
- Go ahead. Just bite him.
- Why you...

503
00:33:28.298 --> 00:33:31.510
You'd better think twice
about the state I'm in.

504
00:33:33.762 --> 00:33:36.640
Okay, point taken. Let go, please.

505
00:33:37.474 --> 00:33:38.726
I got it.

506
00:33:40.310 --> 00:33:41.895
I should just bite you.

507
00:33:42.688 --> 00:33:46.191
I am grateful you kept me around
so I didn't feel lonely.

508
00:33:46.859 --> 00:33:49.737
- But watch your language, okay?
- Okay.

509
00:33:51.530 --> 00:33:54.198
Being rich doesn't make up
for being a jerk.

510
00:33:54.199 --> 00:33:55.701
Right, Boozer?

511
00:33:59.079 --> 00:34:00.580
- Fuck.
- Come on, let's go.

512
00:34:00.581 --> 00:34:01.582
Sure.

513
00:34:20.934 --> 00:34:23.644
Eat up. It might be a long stretch
before we eat again.

514
00:34:23.645 --> 00:34:25.272
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir.

515
00:34:29.318 --> 00:34:30.568
JUNG TAE-HWA
MAY 4, 2025

516
00:34:30.569 --> 00:34:33.530
I'll charge you for this later.
Nothing's free in here.

517
00:34:34.364 --> 00:34:36.575
I really hope I get to pay you later.

518
00:34:37.618 --> 00:34:38.910
Sir.

519
00:34:38.911 --> 00:34:41.371
This is a non-smoking hotel, sir.

520
00:34:42.247 --> 00:34:43.332
He can fine me.

521
00:34:46.752 --> 00:34:48.045
Have a smoke, all of you.

522
00:34:48.962 --> 00:34:50.631
- Pass me one, Jae-yoon.
- Hey.

523
00:34:53.884 --> 00:34:56.303
You can't smoke
in a Michelin-starred restaurant.

524
00:35:00.891 --> 00:35:02.017
Damn it!

525
00:35:05.521 --> 00:35:08.690
You're smoking, too?
Aren't you a staff member?

526
00:35:10.984 --> 00:35:12.778
And you're vaping?

527
00:35:14.279 --> 00:35:16.447
- Shit!
- Are you going somewhere, sir?

528
00:35:16.448 --> 00:35:17.990
I'm getting a drink.

529
00:35:17.991 --> 00:35:21.035
- I'll get it for you, sir.
- No, I can get it myself.

530
00:35:21.036 --> 00:35:22.871
It's getting worse and worse! Fuck!

531
00:35:24.498 --> 00:35:25.331
Paolo.

532
00:35:25.332 --> 00:35:27.793
I'm fucking worried about Korea's future.

533
00:36:10.127 --> 00:36:12.004
- What was that?
- What was that noise?

534
00:36:12.838 --> 00:36:15.423
Sergeant Kim.

535
00:36:15.424 --> 00:36:17.426
Wait, sir.

536
00:36:22.139 --> 00:36:23.140
Sir?

537
00:36:24.224 --> 00:36:25.392
Are you all right?

538
00:36:30.063 --> 00:36:32.941
Sir, we're going to move in.

539
00:36:43.785 --> 00:36:44.620
His legs...

540
00:37:11.605 --> 00:37:13.440
Fuck.

541
00:37:27.537 --> 00:37:29.122
- Sir.
- What?

542
00:37:41.051 --> 00:37:41.969
Shit.

543
00:37:46.431 --> 00:37:47.265
His nose.

544
00:37:47.849 --> 00:37:52.020
The closer the bite is to the head,
the quicker the infection.

545
00:38:28.098 --> 00:38:31.434
We'll head to Seoul Hospital first
then Suseo Station after that.

546
00:38:31.435 --> 00:38:32.602
Seoul Hospital?

547
00:38:33.395 --> 00:38:34.438
My mom's there.

548
00:38:35.230 --> 00:38:38.983
I see. Is she unwell?

549
00:38:38.984 --> 00:38:40.277
Oh, you didn't know?

550
00:38:41.028 --> 00:38:43.697
She owns that hospital.

551
00:38:46.033 --> 00:38:48.909
I have to go to Suseo Station.
Jae-yoon told me to come--

552
00:38:48.910 --> 00:38:51.371
Don't you think he needs to get checked?

553
00:38:51.872 --> 00:38:52.830
What?

554
00:38:52.831 --> 00:38:56.167
We'll get you some help at the hospital,
so don't worry.

555
00:38:56.168 --> 00:38:58.210
You're pretty banged up, too.

556
00:38:58.211 --> 00:39:00.588
It's close to Suseo Station.

557
00:39:00.589 --> 00:39:04.050
I'll drop you off at Suseo Station
after you get treated, okay?

558
00:39:04.051 --> 00:39:05.093
Okay.

559
00:39:10.265 --> 00:39:12.183
Hey, do it out the window.

560
00:39:12.184 --> 00:39:13.934
I need to use the restroom. Pull over.

561
00:39:13.935 --> 00:39:16.187
Where am I supposed to pull over, dumbass?

562
00:39:16.188 --> 00:39:18.981
- Stop the car before I bite you!
- Okay, fine!

563
00:39:18.982 --> 00:39:21.109
I'm pulling over. Shit.

564
00:39:21.902 --> 00:39:25.530
- Damn it, he's fucking crazy.
- Hey.

565
00:39:32.954 --> 00:39:35.832
Is there a restroom nearby?

566
00:39:36.541 --> 00:39:40.169
Does it matter? I can puke anywhere.

567
00:39:40.170 --> 00:39:42.839
That's gross. We're not friends anymore.

568
00:39:44.466 --> 00:39:47.594
I want to go home and eat <i>ramyeon</i>
loaded with black pepper.

569
00:39:48.303 --> 00:39:51.680
You eat it like that, too?
It's the best hangover cure.

570
00:39:51.681 --> 00:39:55.644
You bet I do.
You know what's good, Boozer.

571
00:39:56.228 --> 00:39:58.772
Don't call me Boozer.
I'm totally sober now.

572
00:39:59.689 --> 00:40:01.608
I'm starting to sober up, too.

573
00:40:02.400 --> 00:40:04.402
- I'm going to go home.
- What?

574
00:40:08.615 --> 00:40:11.283
You should come with us
and get your leg checked.

575
00:40:11.284 --> 00:40:13.911
- And Suseo Station--
- No, I'm scared of hospitals.

576
00:40:13.912 --> 00:40:15.162
I hate them.

577
00:40:15.163 --> 00:40:17.123
I'd rather go home and study.

578
00:40:17.124 --> 00:40:19.375
You're going to study?
You're fucking crazy.

579
00:40:19.376 --> 00:40:22.545
The world might recover from this
surprisingly quickly.

580
00:40:22.546 --> 00:40:26.174
If I study while they're distracted,
I'll get ahead of them.

581
00:40:32.514 --> 00:40:35.224
Go before it gets too dangerous.
I'll find my way home.

582
00:40:35.225 --> 00:40:37.935
Okay, take care.
Let's head to the hospital.

583
00:40:37.936 --> 00:40:41.105
Are you sure you'll be okay on your own?

584
00:40:41.106 --> 00:40:42.858
Come on, Boozer.

585
00:40:46.444 --> 00:40:48.112
It's "don't worry," you idiot.

586
00:40:48.113 --> 00:40:51.533
You'd better go home and study hard.
Seems like you need it.

587
00:40:56.454 --> 00:40:58.664
I will, so just get out of here, punk!

588
00:40:58.665 --> 00:40:59.708
What, punk?

589
00:41:00.208 --> 00:41:03.211
Step on the gas, you moron.

590
00:41:07.174 --> 00:41:08.257
Wait.

591
00:41:08.258 --> 00:41:11.386
- Hey, be careful.
- I will.

592
00:41:12.262 --> 00:41:13.471
Be careful out there.

593
00:41:16.349 --> 00:41:18.685
No! Leave them alone!

594
00:41:35.160 --> 00:41:36.369
Will he be okay?

595
00:41:44.669 --> 00:41:46.671
By the way, what was his name?

596
00:41:50.217 --> 00:41:52.552
I should've gotten his name.

597
00:41:55.180 --> 00:41:57.057
He was turning into a zombie.

598
00:41:57.891 --> 00:42:00.769
He couldn't have stayed
with us much longer.

599
00:42:02.771 --> 00:42:04.648
It's time we went our separate ways.

600
00:42:11.780 --> 00:42:12.864
What an idiot.

601
00:42:20.497 --> 00:42:22.874
It's time we went our separate ways.

602
00:42:24.960 --> 00:42:29.339
Hey, stop it. Stay back, damn it!

603
00:42:32.509 --> 00:42:33.760
You fuckers!

604
00:42:37.305 --> 00:42:40.392
Damn, this is way easier than studying.

